The Platos webapp is a Remix application under `apps/webapp`. It serves the dashboard and Platos HTTP API.

## Environment variables and testing

Server environment variables are accessed through [env.server.ts](mdc:apps/webapp/app/env.server.ts), not directly through `process.env` in application modules. Keep service logic independent from environment loading so focused tests can supply explicit options.

Place webapp tests under `apps/webapp/test/` or beside the source when the surrounding package already follows that pattern. Follow [tests.md](mdc:ai/references/tests.md).

## Current boundaries

- Use the current files under `apps/webapp/app/`; do not recreate removed inherited route or `app/v3` paths from old editor guidance.
- The canonical clean tenancy persistence package is `@platos/tenancy-database`.
- Keep external workflow integrations behind adapters. Use Turn for Platos-owned agent work and Job for asynchronous Platos work.
